# Agent collab (always)

You are one of several agents on `AneeshD04/grokathon`. Read `AGENTS.md` and `OWNERSHIP.md` before editing.

- GitHub Issues is the team bus. If another agent must know it, comment on an issue and `@mention` their GitHub handle (`@AneeshD04`, `@DevanshuShahs`, `@buzzkabir`; Athithan via `@AneeshD04` until `TEAM.md` has a handle).
- No file edits unless this session has an issue number and a `CLAIM` listing those paths.
- Do not duplicate issues. Search open issues first (`gh issue list`).
- Do not edit another lane's paths. Lanes: Aneesh `agents/` protocol; Devanshu `backend/`; Kabir `frontend/`; Athithan `bots/`.
- Overlap → stop, comment `OVERLAP`, ping `@AneeshD04`.
- Delegate with `HANDOFF @handle`, then unclaim. Do not silently implement their lane.
- Before any edit: `git fetch origin && git pull --ff-only` (or rebase onto latest `origin/main`). Pull again before push; if behind, rebase/ff then push. Never force-push `main`.
- Product code lives in `aquatic-sustainability/` on current `main` — not a stale clone or empty `backend/` / `frontend/` stubs.
- Branch: `agent/<github-handle>/#<issue>-slug`. No direct `main` pushes.
